From: RNSBox <rnsbox@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] TCPClientInterface: honour a configured bitrate

RNS's TCP client hard-codes the 10 Mbit/s guess and ignores the documented
`bitrate` option. The HaLow modem link is 500 kbit/s (and a remote TCP peer
may be slower), and Reticulum uses this value to size announce caps and link
timeouts. Read the optional key and use it when set.

--- a/RNS/Interfaces/TCPInterface.py
+++ b/RNS/Interfaces/TCPInterface.py
@@ -131,5 +131,9 @@
         self.mode             = RNS.Interfaces.Interface.Interface.MODE_FULL
         self.bitrate          = TCPClientInterface.BITRATE_GUESS
+        if "bitrate" in c:
+            configured_bitrate = c.as_int("bitrate")
+            if configured_bitrate > 0:
+                self.bitrate = configured_bitrate
         
         self.supports_discovery = True
         if max_reconnect_tries == None: self.max_reconnect_tries = TCPClientInterface.RECONNECT_MAX_TRIES
